tive-office-of-united-states", "json_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/491", "raw_name": "OFFICE OF THE UNITED STATES TRADE REPRESENTATIVE", "parent_id": null}], "excerpts": "USTR invites comments from interested parties to inform the development of negotiations with China aimed at optimizing bilateral trade in non-sensitive products in order to promote reciprocity and balance in the U.S.-China trade relationship. In...", "html_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/06/05/2026-11291/request-for-comments-on-the-scope-and-operation-of-a-mechanism-to-promote-reciprocal-managed-trade", "raw_text_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2026/06/05/2026-11291.txt", "document_number": "2026-11291", "publication_date": "2026-06-05", "public_inspection_pdf_url": "https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-11291.pdf?1780577111"}, "title": "Request for Comments on the Scope and Operation of a Mechanism To Promote Reciprocal Managed Trade With China", "agency": "Trade Representative, Office of United States", "source": "federal_register", "summary": "USTR invites comments from interested parties to inform the development of negotiations with China aimed at optimizing bilateral trade in non-sensitive products in order to promote reciprocity and balance in the U.S.-China trade relationship. In particular, comment is sought on the types of non-sensitive products that would benefit from favorable tariff modifications by both sides, and considerations around the design of a new government-to-government mechanism--a U.S.-China Board of Trade--to manage bilateral trade optimization on an ongoing basis.", "category": "geopolitical", "countries": ["China"], "created_at": "2026-10-04T02:29:09.161622+00:00", "source_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/06/05/2026-11291/request-for-comments-on-the-scope-and-operation-of-a-mechanism-to-promote-reciprocal-managed-trade", "external_id": "2026-11291", "duplicate_of": null, "jurisdiction": "Trade Representative, Office of United States · Federal", "effective_date": null, "published_date": "2026-06-05", "on_public_inspection": false, "duplicates_checked_at": null}, {"id": "ead24798-a50a-4d53-aa16-7137ba4b7020", "raw": {"type": "Rule", "title": "Global Benchmark for Efficient Drug Pricing (GLOBE) Model", "pdf_url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-10-02/pdf/2026-20281.pdf", "abstract": "This final rule implements the Global Benchmark for Efficient Drug Pricing Model (GLOBE Model), a new mandatory Medicare payment model under section 1115A of the Social Security Act. The GLOBE Model will test whether a payment model that uses an alternative method for calculating Medicare Part B drug inflation rebate amounts for certain separately payable Medicare Part B drugs and biological products reduces costs for Original Medicare (OM) beneficiaries and the Medicare program while preserving quality of care. The term OM has the same meaning as Medicare fee-for-service and the traditional Medicare program.", "agencies": [{"id": 221, "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/health-and-human-services-department", "name": "Health and Human Services Department", "slug": "health-and-human-services-department", "json_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/221", "raw_name": "DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES", "parent_id": null}, {"id": 45, "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/centers-for-medicare-medicaid-services", "name": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services", "slug": "centers-for-medicare-medicaid-services", "json_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/45", "raw_name": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services", "parent_id": 221}], "excerpts": "This final rule implements the Global Benchmark for Efficient Drug Pricing Model (GLOBE Model), a new mandatory Medicare payment model under section 1115A of the Social Security Act. The GLOBE Model will test whether a payment model that uses an...", "html_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/02/2026-20281/global-benchmark-for-efficient-drug-pricing-globe-model", "raw_text_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2026/10/02/2026-20281.txt", "document_number": "2026-20281", "publication_date": "2026-10-02", "countries_from_full_text": false, "public_inspection_pdf_url": "https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-20281.pdf?1790799310"}, "title": "Global Benchmark for Efficient Drug Pricing (GLOBE) Model", "agency": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services", "source": "federal_register", "summary": "This final rule implements the Global Benchmark for Efficient Drug Pricing Model (GLOBE Model), a new mandatory Medicare payment model under section 1115A of the Social Security Act. The GLOBE Model will test whether a payment model that uses an alternative method for calculating Medicare Part B drug inflation rebate amounts for certain separately payable Medicare Part B drugs and biological products reduces costs for Original Medicare (OM) beneficiaries and the Medicare program while preserving quality of care. The term OM has the same meaning as Medicare fee-for-service and the traditional Medicare program.", "category": "regulatory", "countries": [], "created_at": "2026-10-02T11:00:05.915936+00:00", "source_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/02/2026-20281/global-benchmark-for-efficient-drug-pricing-globe-model", "external_id": "2026-20281", "duplicate_of": null, "jurisdiction": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services · Federal", "effective_date": null, "published_date": "2026-10-02", "on_public_inspection": false, "duplicates_checked_at": null}, {"id": "120778e8-63be-49f9-8f2f-29fdd7ef308f", "raw": {"title": "Oklahoma Corporation Commission - Pipeline Tariff Filing Discontinuation", "agency": "Oklahoma Corporation Commission", "summary": "OCC will no longer accept filings of pipeline tariffs, eliminating a previous filing requirement for certain pipeline operators.", "source_url": "https://oklahoma.gov/occ/divisions/pipeline-safety/pipeline-tariff.html", "jurisdiction": "Oklahoma (state)", "effective_date": "2026-09-01", "published_date": "", "why_it_applies": "Cascade Pipeline Services (test) operates in Oklahoma."}, "title": "Oklahoma Corporation Commission - Pipeline Tariff Filing Discontinuation", "agency": "Oklahoma Corporation Commission", "source": "ai_search", "summary": "OCC will no longer accept filings of pipeline tariffs, eliminating a previous filing requirement for certain pipeline operators.", "category": "regulatory", "countries": [], "created_at": "2026-10-08T22:57:33.079152+00:00", "source_url": "https://oklahoma.gov/occ/divisions/pipeline-safety/pipeline-tariff.html", "external_id": "9d88191d-191e-4ac4-b8ce-e02f9a954dee:https://oklahoma.gov/occ/divisions/pipeline-safety/pipeline-tariff.html", "duplicate_of": null, "jurisdiction": "Oklahoma (state)", "effective_date": "2026-09-01", "published_date": null, "on_public_inspection": false, "duplicates_checked_at": "2026-10-08T23:08:02.497+00:00"}, {"id": "57aecc05-7dfc-454e-9692-c30d9f79cf92", "raw": {"type": "Proposed Rule", "title": "Electronic Disclosure by Group Health Plans Under ERISA", "pdf_url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-07-23/pdf/2026-14917.pdf", "abstract": "This proposed rule sets forth a new, additional safe harbor for group health plan administrators to use electronic media (e.g., email or web portal) to furnish documents and information to participants and beneficiaries of plans subject to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974 (ERISA). This proposal, if finalized, would allow plan administrators who satisfy specified conditions to provide participants and beneficiaries with a notice that certain disclosures will be made available electronically on a website. Individuals who prefer to receive these disclosures on paper will be able to request paper copies and to opt out of electronic delivery entirely. The Department expects that the proposal, if finalized, would improve the effectiveness of the disclosures and significantly reduce the costs and burden to group health plans associated with furnishing many of the recurring disclosures.", "agencies": [{"id": 271, "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/labor-department", "name": "Labor Department", "slug": "labor-department", "json_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/271", "raw_name": "DEPARTMENT OF LABOR", "parent_id": null}, {"id": 131, "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/employee-benefits-security-administration", "name": "Employee Benefits Security Administration", "slug": "employee-benefits-security-administration", "json_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/131", "raw_name": "Employee Benefits Security Administration", "parent_id": 271}], "excerpts": "This proposed rule sets forth a new, additional safe harbor for group health plan administrators to use electronic media (e.g., email or web portal) to furnish documents and information to participants and beneficiaries of plans subject to the Employee...", "html_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/07/23/2026-14917/electronic-disclosure-by-group-health-plans-under-erisa", "raw_text_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2026/07/23/2026-14917.txt", "document_number": "2026-14917", "publication_date": "2026-07-23", "public_inspection_pdf_url": "https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-14917.pdf?1784724317"}, "title": "Electronic Disclosure by Group Health Plans Under ERISA", "agency": "Labor Department", "source": "federal_register", "summary": "This proposed rule sets forth a new, additional safe harbor for group health plan administrators to use electronic media (e.g., email or web portal) to furnish documents and information to participants and beneficiaries of plans subject to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974 (ERISA). This proposal, if finalized, would allow plan administrators who satisfy specified conditions to provide participants and beneficiaries with a notice that certain disclosures will be made available electronically on a website. Individuals who prefer to receive these disclosures on paper will be able to request paper copies and to opt out of electronic delivery entirely. The Department expects that the proposal, if finalized, would improve the effectiveness of the disclosures and significantly reduce the costs and burden to group health plans associated with furnishing many of the recurring disclosures.", "category": "regulatory", "countries": [], "created_at": "2026-09-23T01:15:09.498411+00:00", "source_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/07/23/2026-14917/electronic-disclosure-by-group-health-plans-under-erisa", "external_id": "2026-14917", "duplicate_of": null, "jurisdiction": "Labor Department · Federal", "effective_date": null, "published_date": "2026-07-23", "on_public_inspection": false, "duplicates_checked_at": null}]'::jsonb) on conflict do nothing;
